# Nook and Care — Backend Development Standards

## Project Purpose

Nook and Care is a **senior housing marketplace platform** built with FastAPI.  
The SRS and database schema are defined in [docs/index.qmd](mdc:docs/index.qmd).  
Always consult that document before adding or modifying any entities.

---

## Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | FastAPI |
| ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.x |
| Schemas | Pydantic v2 |
| DB (prod) | PostgreSQL |
| DB (dev) | SQLite |
| Migrations | Alembic |
| Auth | python-jose (JWT) + passlib (bcrypt) |

---

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── main.py               # FastAPI app entry point
├── core/
│   ├── config.py         # Settings via pydantic-settings
│   ├── security.py       # JWT + password hashing
│   ├── dependencies.py   # Shared FastAPI dependencies
│   └── logging.py        # Structured logging config
├── db/
│   ├── base.py           # Imports all models for Alembic
│   ├── session.py        # Engine + SessionLocal + get_db
│   └── init_db.py        # DB initialization helper
├── models/               # SQLAlchemy ORM models (one file per entity/group)
├── schemas/              # Pydantic v2 schemas (one file per entity)
├── crud/                 # Database CRUD operations (one file per entity)
├── services/             # Business logic (one file per domain)
├── api/
│   ├── api_v1.py         # Aggregates all routers under /api/v1
│   └── routers/          # One router file per entity group
├── seed/
│   └── seed_data.py      # Initial data seeding
└── tests/                # pytest test files
```

---

## SQLAlchemy 2.x Model Rules

- Use `Mapped[T]` and `mapped_column()` for all columns — never the old `Column()` style.
- Use `uuid.UUID` as the Python type for UUID primary keys.
- Default PK pattern:
  ```python
  id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(
      UUID(as_uuid=True), primary_key=True, default=uuid.uuid4
  )
  ```
- Timestamps:
  ```python
  created_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now())
  updated_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now(), onupdate=func.now())
  ```
- All models inherit from `Base` (defined in `db/session.py`).
- Every model file must be imported in `db/base.py` so Alembic can discover it.

---

## Pydantic v2 Schema Rules

- Every entity has four schemas: `EntityBase`, `EntityCreate`, `EntityUpdate`, `EntityRead`.
- `EntityRead` must include `model_config = ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)`.
- `EntityUpdate` fields must all be `Optional[T] = None`.
- Use `uuid.UUID` for UUID fields, `datetime` for timestamps.

---

## CRUD Layer Rules

- Each CRUD module lives at `src/crud/crud_<entity>.py`.
- Functions: `create`, `get_by_id`, `get_all` (skip/limit pagination), `update`, `delete`.
- Use SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()` style — never `session.query()`.
- Return `None` (not exception) when a record is not found in `get_by_id`.

---

## Services Layer Rules

- Business logic (workflow, validation, calculations) lives in `src/services/`.
- Routers must call services — no business logic inside router functions.
- Services receive a `db: Session` parameter and return domain objects or Pydantic schemas.

---

## Router Rules

- Thin routers: validate input, call service/CRUD, return response.
- Always use `Annotated` dependency injection:
  ```python
  db: Annotated[Session, Depends(get_db)]
  ```
- Return `404` when entity not found, `400` for validation failures.
- Tag all routers for Swagger grouping.

---

## API Versioning

- All routes are prefixed `/api/v1/`.
- Routers are registered in `src/api/api_v1.py`.
- Swagger UI is available at `/swagger`.

---

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Model class | PascalCase | `ListingAmenity` |
| Table name | snake_case | `listing_amenities` |
| Schema class | PascalCase + suffix | `ListingCreate` |
| CRUD module | `crud_<entity>.py` | `crud_listing.py` |
| Service module | `<domain>_service.py` | `listing_service.py` |
| Router module | `<entity>.py` | `listings.py` |

---

## Environment Variables

Required in `.env`:

```
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./dev.db           # dev
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...             # prod
SECRET_KEY=<random-32-byte-hex>
ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60
ENVIRONMENT=development
```

---

## Running the API

```bash
uvicorn src.main:app --reload
```

Swagger: http://localhost:8000/swagger
